1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
Everybody plants a tree.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Nobody finds out what happened to it.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
A birthday.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
A school drive.

5
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,000
A company afternoon.

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,000
They plant it, they take the photo, they post it,

7
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
and that is where it ends.

8
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The planting is an event.

9
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
The keeping alive is a year.

10
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,000
So how much of it lives?

11
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
India's national auditor went and looked.

12
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Of a two point eight million hectare target,

13
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,000
about five percent was achieved.

14
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
At seventy percent of the sites,

15
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,000
no improvement in tree cover at all.

16
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
One site reported two thousand plantings.

17
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Thirty were found.

18
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,000
None had survived.

19
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,000
And here is the part that explains the rest.

20
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Four out of five plantation records did not say what was

21
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
planted, where it stood, or whether it lived.

22
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Nobody was ever asked to keep one.

23
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Planting is not the solution.

24
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
Keeping it alive is.

25
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
And we already pay people to do boring things.

26
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Pay a credit card bill on time, and you earn points.

27
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Water the tree you planted last year,

28
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,000
and nothing happens at all.

29
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Rooted pays you for keeping it alive.

30
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
The tulsi on the balcony.

31
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
The money plant in the living room.

32
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The lemon by the kitchen window.

33
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The sapling from last month's drive.

34
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Same app, same schedule.

35
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:16,000
You do not have to know anything about the plant.

36
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Every plant carries its own coordinates,

37
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
and the schedule moves with the weather over it.

38
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Rain pushes the next watering out.

39
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Heat pulls it in.

40
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
And you are not expected to know any of it.

41
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:30,000
When to feed it, what to spray, how often to water.

42
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,000
It tells you, on the day.

43
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Water, on this species own interval,

44
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:37,000
moved by the rain and the heat.

45
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Feeding, with what this plant wants, and less than you think,

46
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
because what the roots do not take ends up in the groundwater.

47
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Pests, with what goes wrong with this species,

48
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
and the mildest thing that works.

49
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:51,000
And a weekly look while it establishes,

50
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
which is when losing it is least visible.

51
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Every plant also carries a health score.

52
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Thriving, steady, watch it, at risk,

53
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:02,000
and one sentence saying what moved it.

54
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:05,000
It does not read the leaves and call the plant sick.

55
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
A yellow leaf has a dozen causes.

56
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,000
The camera then tells you what would make the shot pass.

57
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Out loud,

58
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:15,000
because whoever is doing this is holding a watering can.

59
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:23,000
It reads the frame twice a second, on the phone,

60
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,000
uploading nothing.

61
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Tilt down so the soil is in frame.

62
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Then the ring turns green.

63
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Then it is checked, and every check says the number it measured.

64
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
It came off the camera.

65
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The time is ours.

66
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:38,000
The location matches where this plant was registered.

67
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
And soil five percent darker than that plant's own dry baseline.

68
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Measured, not guessed.

69
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:46,000
This is the one that matters.

70
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,000
If any plant earned points, the points would be worth nothing.

71
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
So OpenCV matches keypoints against the plant's first

72
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,000
photograph, and asks whether they agree on one viewpoint.

73
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
The same plant returns four hundred and eighty five.

74
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:03,000
A different plant of the same species, in a similar pot,

75
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
returns four.

76
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Registering a plant checks the photograph before it accepts it.

77
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Point it at a notebook and it says so.

78
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,000
An object scores nought point two percent.

79
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The weakest real plant scored nine.

80
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Point it at a plant and it works out what it is.

81
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:24,000
Seventy-eight species, searched by local name.

82
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
A plant cannot wait for you to remember it.

83
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,000
So Rooted does not wait to be opened.

84
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:33,000
When a task comes due, the same message goes out on WhatsApp,

85
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
email and text.

86
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
A name, a plant and a date go to the server.

87
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
No photographs, no coordinates.

88
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Organisations spend heavily on planting drives,

89
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,000
and get back a photograph from day one.

90
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Rooted produces the record of what survived,

91
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
every point traceable to one verified task.

92
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:53,000
That record funds the rewards.

93
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,000
The offers are stand-ins,

94
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
because naming a real company would put words in their mouth.

95
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
And somebody is already paying for all of this.

96
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:05,000
Indian companies put forty thousand crore rupees into social

97
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
spending in a single year.

98
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Three thousand four hundred crore of that went into

99
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
environmental work, up forty percent in one year.

100
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
And above ten crore,

101
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,000
the law already asks them for an independent assessment of what

102
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,000
the money achieved.

103
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
The money is there.

104
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,000
The proof is the part nobody can produce.

105
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Rooted makes it, one verified task at a time,

106
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
by the person who did the work.

107
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:30,000
We reward people for spending money.

108
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Rooted rewards them for keeping something alive.

109
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Plant it.

110
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Keep it.

111
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Get paid for it.

112
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Rooted is already everywhere.

113
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
It opens on any phone and sits on the home screen like an app.

114
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
No store, nothing to install.

115
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,000
Scan the left one to use it.

116
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Scan the right one to read every line of it.

117
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Nothing in here reports a number it did not measure.